{
  "bullets": [
    {
      "text": "GitHub now explicitly treats AI-generated outputs as collected personal data and establishes new lawful bases and processing purposes to use user data for training and improving artificial intelligence and machine learning technologies.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "hunk": "h2",
          "side": "added",
          "quote": "- User Content and Files: When you use our Services, we collect Personal Data included as part of the information you provide such as code, inputs, AI outputs, text, documents, images, or feedback."
        },
        {
          "hunk": "h5",
          "side": "added",
          "quote": "- Product Development and Improvement: We use Personal Data to develop and improve our products, services, and technologies, including artificial intelligence and machine learning technologies. This includes improving features, developing new offerings, enhancing safety and security capabilities, and training models. We apply appropriate technical safeguards, including aggregation and de-identification techniques where feasible, to protect your privacy while enabling these improvements."
        },
        {
          "hunk": "h8",
          "side": "added",
          "quote": "- Legitimate Interests: We process data for purposes that are in our legitimate interests, such as securing our Services, communicating with you, and developing and improving our Services, which include artificial intelligence and machine learning technologies. This is done only when these interests are not overridden by your data protection rights or your fundamental rights and freedoms."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Data shared with GitHub’s affiliates, including Microsoft, may now be utilized for artificial intelligence and machine learning product development and improvement, expanding how affiliate partners can leverage user information.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "hunk": "h6",
          "side": "added",
          "quote": "- Affiliates: Personal Data may be shared with GitHub affiliates, including Microsoft, to facilitate customer service, marketing and advertising, order fulfillment, billing, technical support, legal and compliance obligations, product development and improvement (including training and improving artificial intelligence and machine learning technologies), and for other purposes described in their respective privacy statements. When we share data with affiliates, they will process it in accordance with applicable law and their privacy commitments."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The privacy policy removes its own detailed list of circumstances under which GitHub personnel may access private repositories, instead deferring entirely to the GitHub Terms of Service for those rules.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "hunk": "h7",
          "side": "removed",
          "quote": "If your GitHub account has private repositories, you control the access to that information. GitHub personnel does not access private repository information without your consent except as provided in this Privacy Statement and for:\n- security purposes\n- automated scanning or manual review for known vulnerabilities, active malware, or other content known to violate our Terms of Service\n- to assist the repository owner with a support matter\n- to maintain the integrity of the Services, or\n- to comply with our legal obligations if we have reason to believe the contents are in violation of the law.\nGitHub will provide you with notice regarding private repository access unless doing so is prohibited by law or if GitHub acted in response to a security threat or other risk to security."
        },
        {
          "hunk": "h7",
          "side": "added",
          "quote": "If your GitHub account has private repositories, our ability and rights to access private repository information is set forth in Section E (Private Repositories) of the GitHub Terms of Service."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The policy’s effective date has been pushed forward to April 2026, indicating a longer transition or review period before these updated terms take effect.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "hunk": "h1",
          "side": "added",
          "quote": "Effective date: April 27, 2026"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "GitHub broadens the scope of third-party data collection by removing the specific example of acquiring information from public GitHub repositories, leaving the category open-ended.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "hunk": "h4",
          "side": "removed",
          "quote": "- Publicly Available Sources: We may acquire information about you from publicly available sources like public GitHub repositories."
        },
        {
          "hunk": "h4",
          "side": "added",
          "quote": "- Publicly Available Sources: We may acquire information about you from publicly available sources."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "bullets": [
    {
      "text": "The policy clarifies that privacy settings specifically encompass \"history and personalization controls\" and reframes user choice around saving data to your account rather than merely controlling data collection.",
